> tlp0: receive error: MII error
> tlp0: receive error: dribbling bit
> tlp0: receive error: CRC error

Seen that too, some times. At one time I suspected bad cabling (or a losing
connector), but I've never realy found out (the machine this happened with
died, and other tulip cars I have don't show the symptom).

> I was just wondering whether there might be any difference
> or advantage in using de driver or tlp?

The de driver is older and replaced by the tlp driver. Generally tlp provides
better results - but you might try it. For me this happened (IIRC) with both
drivers.

> Or might it be sensible to replace tlp1 with a spare rtk NIC?

Uh oh - tulip chipsets are considered pretty good, while rtk ones are just
cheap. I wouldn't swap a tulip for a rtk.

Martin


